# Copy to .pii-patterns.local and fill in your own identifiers.
# .pii-patterns.local is gitignored — safe to store names/handles here.
#
# Format: one pattern per line, case-insensitive regex.
#         pattern|human-readable-reason
#
# Lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored.
#
# Add YOUR OWN private identifiers that must never appear in commits:

# --- personal name fragments (example placeholders — replace with yours) ---
# yourfirstname|personal first-name fragment
# yourlastname|personal last-name fragment

# --- your primary GitHub/GitLab handle (if it should NOT appear in code) ---
# \byourhandle\b|personal handle

# --- private project names you're NOT publishing here ---
# \bproject-alpha\b|private project name
# \bproject-beta\b|private project name

# --- your org's private infrastructure (replace with real patterns) ---
# internal-service\.example\.com|private infra hostname
# \b[A-Z]{4,10}-[0-9]{4,8}\b|internal ticket ID

# --- keep this file uncommitted ---
# Confirm .pii-patterns.local is in .gitignore. Running
# `grep pii-patterns .gitignore` should return a match.
